    "created_at": "2016-02-01T23:20:31Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-02-01T23:20:31Z",
    "body": "Synthetic click events totally cause actions in other cases and need to for web compat, so I think a note about this would be a very good idea.\n\nBut even worse, from the point of view of the patch under discussion, is that my \"synthetic, clearly\" comment is wrong.  The event can be non-synthetic, but the `<summary>` can still be `display:none` or removed from the DOM or moved to a different `<details>` or whatever whatever by the time the default action is happening....\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
