    "created_at": "2016-03-18T18:04:54Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-18T18:04:54Z",
    "body": "@annevk We've locked down a bunch of \"synthetic events having side effects\" issues, but `click` has always been special since many of those cases are required for web-compat.  Do you guys know if the specific cases are enumerated somewhere?  Perhaps we could replace our general \"allow synthetic clicks to execute the default action\" logic with something that's per-scenario.  @dtapuska, thoughts?\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
