    "created_at": "2016-03-18T18:19:55Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-18T18:19:55Z",
    "body": "The appropriate code is in the [EventDispatcher](https://code.google.com/p/chromium/codesearch#chromium/src/third_party/WebKit/Source/core/events/EventDispatcher.cpp&sq=package:chromium&type=cs&l=214&rcl=1458300685). Our logic is if it is a mouse event with type \"click\"; when we allow untrusted events to fire. Certainly doing targeting checks is not difficult; the problem is identifying the rule-set for compatiblity .\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
